// Putting a concept's items in the order that suits the learner. The planner often
// deals several items of one concept into a session (one per round); which of them
// comes first matters, because what a beginner needs first (an error hunt, a
// choice) is not what an expert needs first (a proof, a counterexample). These
// helpers find the main-set rows of one concept, give each row's item a sort key
// (the kind's rank for the learner's level times 10000, plus the item's
// difficulty, so equal kinds go easiest first) and are used by order_put.id to
// hand the items back to those same rows in key order. The rows keep their places
// in the session, so the concepts stay interleaved.

plan_concept_rows(Plan_book plan_book, Plan_session plan_session, int plan_concept_number) {
  int[] plan_rows_found = [];
  int plan_at = 0;
  while (plan_at < len(plan_session.ids)) {
    if (plan_session.phases[plan_at] == "main" && plan_first_concept(plan_book, list_string_index(plan_book.catalog.items, plan_session.ids[plan_at])) == plan_concept_number) {
      push(plan_rows_found, plan_at);
    }
    plan_at = plan_at + 1;
  }
} return int[] plan_rows_found;
